      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION:",
          "content": "The clinical and epidemiological aspects associated with Portuguese man-of-war envenomation were investigated and characterized."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "METHODS:",
          "content": "Data from recorded envenomation events between 2005 and 2013 were provided by the GBMar (Group of Firemen Maritime of Maranhão State) and SEMUSC (Municipal Secretary of Security with Citizenship)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "RESULTS:",
          "content": "Most victims were children, and clinical manifestations included intense pain, edema, erythema, and rare systemic manifestations."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS:",
          "content": "The envenomation events were predictable and based on patterns involving multiple factors (environmental and/or human behavior); however, the initially applied measures did not match the current recommendations of the Health Ministry of Brazil."
        }
      ]},
